# Never convert line endings, in either direction.
#
# The repo stores LF. Windows autocrlf was rewriting the working copy to CRLF on any
# checkout, stash, or merge — which breaks latte-tests.js instantly and silently, because
# every span anchor it extracts from the HTML is written with '\n'. The failure looks like a
# wholesale regression (anchor extraction throws) rather than a line-ending problem, which
# is exactly the wrong signal to hand someone mid-debug.
#
# `-text` means the working tree bytes and the repo bytes are always identical.
* -text
